The legal texts come from the Biblioteca del Congreso Nacional de Chile:

  Fuente: Biblioteca del Congreso Nacional de Chile, LeyChile (www.bcn.cl/leychile),
  https://www.bcn.cl/leychile, retrieved 28 October 2026.

BCN publishes no licence for LeyChile. They are official legal texts of the Republic of Chile. Chile's copyright law
(Ley 17.336) has no express exclusion for legal texts, so their copyright status is not confirmed here; they are
reproduced with the attribution above.

Changes made by Lexifina: each version was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per line;
spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; LeyChile's amendment notes and BCN's editorial notes were removed from the
text and used only to credit the amending norm; and the versions were arranged as git commits credited to the norms
that made each change. The wording of the law was not changed. BCN does not endorse this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
